    "云水纹样": "Cloud & water",
    "云气、波涛、流水等自然气象的纹样化，贯穿商周到明清。云纹由商周云雷纹演化出卷云、如意云、团云、朵云诸式；水纹则有波浪纹、落花流水纹、海水江崖纹。海水江崖纹以\"海水\"与\"江崖\"组合，取\"江山永固、福山寿海\"之义，是明清龙袍下摆的经典纹样。云水象征绵延不息与福泽绵长。": "The patterning of clouds, waves and flowing water runs from the Shang and Zhou through the Ming and Qing. Cloud patterns evolved from Shang–Zhou cloud-thunder into rolled cloud, ruyi cloud, round cloud and dab cloud forms; water patterns include wave, fallen-flower-on-flowing-water and sea-and-cliff patterns. The sea-and-cliff pattern combines “sea” and “cliff” to convey “rivers and mountains enduring, mountains of blessing and sea of longevity”; it is the classic motif on the hem of Ming–Qing dragon robes. Clouds and water stand for unending continuity and lasting good fortune.",
    "依据《中国纹样史》分类体系。海水江崖纹释义参见明清服饰纹样通行考据；真迹图版见 Jones 原书海马踏浪、蝙蝠祥云诸版（图版 29）。": "Based on the classification system of A History of Chinese Ornament. On the sea-and-cliff pattern see the standard scholarship on Ming–Qing dress patterns; original plates from Jones — sea-horse riding the wave and bat-and-auspicious-cloud designs (plate 29).",
    "云水": "cloud and water",
    "云纹": "cloud pattern",
