    "海水江崖": "sea and cliff",
    "落花流水": "fallen flowers on flowing water",
    "瑞兽神异": "Mythic beasts",
    "龙、凤、饕餮、麒麟、海马等神异瑞兽，源于上古图腾崇拜与礼制，承载威严、祥瑞与庇护之义。饕餮纹是商周青铜器最具代表性的纹样，以兽面为中心、双目突出，对称严整；龙纹自商周夔龙演化至明清五爪金龙，成为皇权象征。瑞兽纹常见于礼器、服饰与建筑彩画，是\"器以载道\"的典型。": "Dragons, phoenixes, taotie, qilin, sea-horses and other mythical auspicious beasts derive from ancient totem worship and ritual order, bearing meanings of authority, auspiciousness and protection. The taotie is the most representative motif on Shang–Zhou bronzes: a beast face at the centre with protruding eyes, strictly symmetrical; dragon patterns evolved from Shang–Zhou kui-dragons to the five-clawed golden dragon of the Ming and Qing, becoming a symbol of imperial power. Auspicious-beast patterns appear on ritual vessels, dress and architectural painting, a classic case of “the vessel carrying the way”.",
    "依据《中国纹样史》分类体系与商周青铜器纹饰通行考据；真迹图版见 Jones 原书游龙边饰（图版 64）等版。": "Based on the classification system of A History of Chinese Ornament and standard scholarship on Shang–Zhou bronze decoration; original plates from Jones — roaming-dragon border (plate 64) and others.",
    "瑞兽": "auspicious beast",
    "神异": "mythical",
