    "文字吉语": "Characters and auspicious words",
    "寿、喜、福、禄、卍等吉字被纹样化处理，笔画拉长变形、嵌入几何骨架，成为可平铺的装饰单元，是\"图必有意、意必吉祥\"最直接的表达。典型者如\"寿\"字纹（团寿、长寿、百寿）、\"囍\"字纹、万字不到头（卍字连续）。本作品当前图库暂无文字吉语类真迹图版，前端会自动隐藏该谱系而非展示空分类。": "Auspicious characters such as shou (longevity), xi (joy), fu (blessing), lu (emolument) and wan are treated as patterns, with strokes stretched and deformed and set into geometric skeletons to become tileable decorative units — the most direct expression of “every picture has a meaning, every meaning is auspicious”. Typical examples are the shou character (round, long and hundred-shou forms), the double-xi character, and the endless wan (linked wan characters). The current plate library of this work has no original plates in the character-and-auspicious-word lineage, so the front end hides that lineage automatically rather than showing an empty category.",
    "依据《中国纹样史》分类体系。本作品图库现状说明见 docs/交接摘要.md。": "Based on the classification system of A History of Chinese Ornament. On the current state of this work's plate library see docs/交接摘要.md.",
